; exit 31 (see .exit)
; The facts an error-propagating loop stands on. They pull in different
; directions - one is about where the RECURSION sits, one about where
; the ERROR VALUE sits, and one is a cost nothing currently reclaims.
;
; Measured 2026-08-16, before `docs/error-model.md` specified anything,
; because a propagation model that cannot survive a loop is not a model.
;
; 1. WHERE THE RECURSION SITS. `(match (recur ...) ...)` is not a tail
;    call - the match is what the call returns INTO - so the loop
;    conversion does not fire and each step costs a frame. Measured at
;    32 bytes of stack per frame: that shape survives 250,000
;    iterations and dies of SIGSEGV at 262,144, which is 8 MiB exactly.
;    The shape below is the other one: the fallible call is the
;    SCRUTINEE and the recursion is what the `Good` arm ANSWERS, so the
;    self call is in tail position inside the arm and converts.
;    1,000,000 iterations here, four times past the cliff.
;
;    This is the happy direction, and it decides the surface: a
;    propagation form desugars to `(match e ((Bad ..) ..) ((Good x)
;    BODY))` with the continuation in the ARM, which is the shape that
;    converts. Writing it the other way round is what does not work.
;
; 2. WHERE THE ERROR VALUE SITS. The tail-call release boundary
;    (MM-LIFE-2c event 4) releases a reference parameter across the
;    jump, and a `data` block births owned at count 1. Constructed
;    INLINE in the tail-call argument the boundary retain takes it to 2
;    and the single release returns it to 1 - never 0, so it never
;    files. Bound to a `let` first, the frame's scope release spends the
;    birth count and the loop is flat. Measured over 2000 iterations
;    each carrying a fresh 32-byte String: inline 288,176 bytes,
;    returned from a function 288,176, let-bound 176.
;
;    Term 4 asserts this over a POLYMORPHIC error type applied at
;    concrete arguments, because that is what a `Result` is and because
;    `fldClass` classifies an applied type by its head - a monomorphic
;    probe would not have asked the question.
;
; 3. WHAT NOTHING RECLAIMS, and why term 8 is a control rather than a
;    flatness claim. The block a fallible call RETURNS is not reclaimed
;    under any spelling: matching the call directly and let-binding it
;    first both leak exactly 32 bytes per call - one `Res` block -
;    measured at 10,000 and 50,000 iterations, both 32.0 bytes/iter on
;    the nose. So term 8 asserts the CONTROL instead: the same loop
;    with no `Res` in it is flat, which is what attributes those 32
;    bytes to the error value and not to the loop. A fixture asserting
;    the leak would have to be rewritten the day it is fixed; a control
;    that isolates it does not. The defect is registered in
;    `docs/error-model.md` ERR-MEM-4.
;
;    That measurement also fixed the metric. A `memAlloc` address delta
;    is only meaningful BELOW the allocator's chunk size: the same
;    loop read 32.0 bytes/iter at 10,000 and 50,000 and 795.7 at
;    100,000, because at ~3.2 MB the bump crossed into a chunk that is
;    not contiguous with the last and the raw subtraction counted the
;    gap. Every delta below stays well under it.
;
;   16  the arm-tail propagation loop completes 1,000,000 iterations
;    8  the same loop with no Result in it allocates nothing
;    4  a reference-carrying error value, let-bound at the boundary, is
;       reclaimed - 2000 iterations, each allocating a fresh String
;    2  an error answers unchanged through the loop it exits
;    1  every step above ran
;
; Ablations, run 2026-08-16. Move the recursion into the scrutinee:
; SIGSEGV and no exit code at all, which is why term 16 is a completion
; and not a value. Drop the `let` in `carry` and construct the error
; inline: term 4 goes to 0 and that bump moves 288,176.
(import Str)

(import Mem)

(data Res (a e)
  (Good a)
  (Bad e))

(:: b2i (-> Bool Int))

(fn (b2i x)
  (if x
    1
    0
  )
)

(:: wide (-> Int String))

(fn (wide k) (strDup "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"))

; a fallible step that does not, in fact, fail here
(:: step (-> Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (step n)
  (if (< n 0)
    (Bad n)
    (Good 1)
  )
)

; the same step with no error value, for term 8's control
(:: stepPlain (-> Int Int))

(fn (stepPlain n) 1)

; THE SHAPE. The fallible call is the scrutinee; the recursion is the
; Good arm's answer, in tail position, and converts to a loop.
(:: total (-> Int Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (total n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    (Good acc)
    (match (step n)
      ((Bad e) (Bad e))
      ((Good v) (total (- n 1) (+ acc v)))
    )
  )
)

; term 8's control: identical loop, no Res constructed
(:: totalPlain (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (totalPlain n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (totalPlain (- n 1) (+ acc (stepPlain n)))
  )
)

; a loop carrying a reference in the error payload, let-bound so the
; frame may release it
(:: carry (-> (Res Int String) Int Int))

(fn (carry r n)
  (if (<= n 0)
    0
    (let ((next (Bad (wide n))))
      (carry next (- n 1))
    )
  )
)

; an error raised mid-loop must answer unchanged, not be re-wrapped
(:: failAt (-> Int Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (failAt n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    (Good acc)
    (match (if (== n 500)
      (Bad 77)
      (Good 1)
    )
      ((Bad e) (Bad e))
      ((Good v) (failAt (- n 1) (+ acc v)))
    )
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let (
    (mut acc 0)
    (mut steps 0)
  )
    {
      (set acc (+
        acc        (*
          16          (b2i
            (==
              (match (total 1000000 0)
                ((Good x) x)
                ((Bad e) (- 0 1))
              )              1000000
            )
          )
        )
      ))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (let ((a1 (memAlloc 8)))
        {
          (totalPlain 100000 0)
          (let ((a2 (memAlloc 8)))
            (set acc (+ acc (* 8 (b2i (< (- a2 a1) 4096)))))
          )
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        }
      )
      (let ((b1 (memAlloc 8)))
        {
          (carry (Bad (wide 0)) 2000)
          (let ((b2 (memAlloc 8)))
            (set acc (+ acc (* 4 (b2i (< (- b2 b1) 4096)))))
          )
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        }
      )
      (set acc (+
        acc        (*
          2          (b2i
            (==
              (match (failAt 1000 0)
                ((Good x) x)
                ((Bad e) e)
              )              77
            )
          )
        )
      ))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (if (== steps 4)
        (+ acc 1)
        acc
      )
    }
  )
)
